    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_71d55491",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: perfect_girls_dont_exi; hasOverallIntent: Mysogynous; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a woman in a revealing outfit, being directed by a man holding a firearm, with the text 'perfect girls don't exi' (likely meant to be 'exist'). The scene, combined with the text, frames the woman as an object of male gaze or control, reinforcing harmful stereotypes about women's bodies and roles. The juxtaposition of the text with the visual of a woman in a bikini and tactical gear, while being directed by a man with a weapon, implies that women are not 'perfect' because they are sexualized or objectified, which is a misogynistic trope. The meme uses the visual of the woman's body and the man's authoritative gesture to suggest that women are inherently flawed or incomplete, which is a form of misogynous messaging. The intent is to trivialize or dismiss the idea of 'perfect' women by implying that such an ideal is unattainable or undesirable, while simultaneously objectifying the woman in the image.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_70cd9d90"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
